# F1-APP-ST Project Structure

This rule outlines the directory structure and organization of the F1-APP-ST React Native project - a cross-platform mobile application.

## Project Overview

**F1-APP-ST** is a React Native application that provides:
- Cross-platform mobile experience (iOS/Android)
- Multi-language support (CN/TH/VN)
- Gaming and betting features
- Live chat functionality
- User authentication and profiles

## Root Directory Structure

```
F1-APP-ST/
├── android/            # 🤖 Android platform specific code
├── ios/               # 🍎 iOS platform specific code
├── src/               # 📱 Main application source code
├── scripts/           # 🔧 Build and utility scripts
├── patches/           # 🔄 Package patches
├── package/           # 📦 Package documentation
├── __tests__/         # 🧪 Test files
├── app.json           # 📋 React Native app configuration
├── babel.config.js    # 🔧 Babel configuration
└── package.json       # 📦 Dependencies and scripts
```

## Source Code Structure (`/src/`)

**Purpose**: Main application logic and components

```
src/
├── actions/           # 📡 API calls and data fetching
├── components/        # 🎨 Reusable UI components
├── containers/        # 📄 Screen components and page logic
├── images/           # 🖼️ Static image assets
├── lib/              # 🛠️ Utility functions and helpers
├── locales/          # 🌐 Internationalization files
├── App.js            # 🚀 Main application entry point
└── CodePushIos.json  # 📱 iOS CodePush configuration
```

